# Reference counting and arrays hold to a model of what the runtime says
# they mean, on every case counting.cpp draws: after each operation the
# runtime's live cells, each live object's count and exclusivity, each
# slot's word and the static cells agree with the model, wide cells, odd
# words in slots, arrays held by boxes, view copies and memo cells
# included; at a case's end nothing it made is live. Each run draws from a
# fresh seed, which a failure names; then the property runs with a planted
# fault (the model blind to a wide cell's slots past what objs counts) and
# must catch it.
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
. "$root/harness/prop/prop.sh"
prop_build "$here/counting.cpp" "$work/counting" || exit 0
# 10000 cases ran in 0.3 s on the host build of the runtime for arm64
# macOS; the owner's build of both targets confirms they end well within
# step_limit.
prop_run "$work/counting" --cases 10000
